We aim to enhance the onboarding process by introducing a user-friendly feature that enables users to navigate backward through the steps using a simple button.

🎯 Requirements:
Basic experience with Vue.js.

✅ Task summary:

- [x] Ask to be assigned on the issue by commenting
- [ ] The current next button resides in `OnboardingBuilder.vue`. You will have to implement something similar to how "next" button (`NextButton.vue`) works. 
- [ ] Make a component called `BackButton` in @/apps/dashboard/views/onboarding/components/ directory. When clicked it should emit an event which should get caught in `OnboardingBuilder.vue`. 
- [ ] `currentStep` variable in `OnboardingBuilder.vue` is how we control which step to show to users. So decrease it by 1 when back button is clicked. To make sure this value doesn't go out of bounds do not show back button in the first step.
